# PLACEHOLDER -- Hemp Shelf: vanilla's oak shelf, retoned to hemp planks.
#
# The MATRIX is vanilla `block/oak_shelf.png` (32x32, the shelf's whole UV sheet) taken
# verbatim, so every shelf model part lands on the texel it expects. Only the colours are
# ours: each oak tone was moved from oak_planks.png's luminance range (83-161) onto
# hemp_planks.png's (81-156) and coloured along the hemp planks ramp -- the planks' own
# seven tones plus the two deepest shadows of hemp_planks_door. So the shelf is the same
# wood as the planks it is crafted from, down to the recesses that hold the items.
#
# To retone: change the ramp and redo the luminance mapping for every entry at once. Do
# not hand-edit single entries -- they are a monotone ramp and will band if they stop
# being one. The [note] about the colour count is vanilla's own: oak_shelf.png has 42.

@palette hemp_planks
. = none
1 = 4B462E
2 = 5A5236
3 = 635C3C
4 = 6C6541
5 = 7F764C
6 = 80774D
7 = 847B50
